 ### 2026-10-08T09:20:00Z · agent
 
 2026-10-08 final: phone kubectl bridge working with founder-phone SA (cluster-admin token), served at http://100.98.58.115:9999/estate-cluster.yaml. exec auth kubeconfig doesn't work with InKuber; static ServiceAccount token is the fix. /fleet left public (API gated). Memory committed.
+
+### 2026-10-08T16:13:33Z · agent
+
+Audited the LiteLLM efficiency layer and verified Claude Code's actual routing live (2026-10-08). Router (com.estate.litellm-front + litellm-local-4001) is up, /health/liveliness 200, efficiency_gateway/request_ceiling/anthropic_beta_passthrough callbacks registered proxy-wide in llm/config.yaml so every call incl. claude-* inherits them. The keyless claude-* wildcard lane (no api_key, zero declared cost) confirms Max-subscription passthrough per docs/onboarding/claude-max-passthrough.md. Confirmed THIS session's live process env has ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4000 + ANTHROPIC_CUSTOM_HEADERS (litellm virtual key), sourced from CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=~/.estate/harness/cc/settings.json -- NOT ~/.claude/settings.json, which no longer exists. All 4 shell profiles (.zshrc/.bashrc/.bash_profile/.zprofile) export CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR to the harness path, so this covers every Claude Code process estate-wide, not just this session. Two real defects found: (1) router-doctor.py's 'settings' check hardcodes ~/.claude/settings.json and will always FAIL/BROKEN since the estate moved off that path -- a stale check giving a false negative. (2) live settings.json has model=opus, not the founder-mandated opusplan (2026-09-28 ruling, 'must never be changed again'). Also found via router-doctor's own e2e probe: the keychain 'Claude Code-credentials' Max OAuth token is expired, and a real passthrough call to api.anthropic.com through the router returned 401 -- yet this live interactive session kept working normally, implying its in-process token is not the same one router-doctor reads from keychain. Wrote all four facts to the graph. Not yet fixed: router-doctor path, model=opus, expired keychain token -- left for the founder/next session to decide since each needs a call outside this audit's scope.
